<title>USA: Cheesecake Factory founder dies.</title>
<headline>Cheesecake Factory founder dies.</headline>
<dateline>CALABASAS HILLS, Calif. 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cheesecake Factory Inc said its founder, Evelyn Overton, died on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Overton, 75, founded the company in 1972 with her husband, Oscar Overton and their son, David Overton, the company's current chairman, president and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Her estimated 9.5 percent stake in the company will remain in the family.</p>
<p>&quot;My mother started our business by baking cheesecakes in the basement of our home for friends and relatives,&quot; David Overton said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;From this very humble beginning, our combined restaurant and bakery sales should exceed $150 million this year. All of this was made possible by the entrepreneurial energy, drive, enthusiasm, attention to quality and detail, and creativity of my mother,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
